(\ref{lemma_bounds2_psipr}) By Lemma~\ref{lemma_expectation} and Lemma~\ref{lemma_terms}, we have $$\psi_{p_r}-K=O(q_r^2\alpha M+q_rM^2+(n_k-K)M/\alpha).$$ By (\ref{lemma_bounds2_qr}), we have $q_r=O((\alpha-k-r)/\alpha)$, so (\ref{lemma_bounds2_nrnk}) gives $$\frac{\psi_{p_r}-K}{n_{\alpha-r}-K}=O\left(\frac{(\alpha-k-r)M+M^2}{(\alpha-r)\alpha}+\frac{(n_k-K)M/\alpha}{n_{\alpha-r}-K}\right).$$ The result follows, since $\alpha-k-r\leq\alpha-r$ and $n_k-K\leq n_{\alpha-r}-K$.

(\ref{lemma_sums_1}) For $k+1=o(\alpha-r)$, Lemma~\ref{lemma_bounds2}~(\ref{lemma_bounds2_nrk},\ref{lemma_bounds2_qr}) gives $$\frac{q_r^2}{n_{\alpha-r}-K}=\left(1+O\left(\frac{k+1}{\alpha-r}\right)\right)\tfrac{2}{\ell}\alpha^{-2}=\tfrac{P}{\alpha}+O\left(\frac{M}{(\alpha-r)\alpha^2}\right).$$ For the sum, we get
