	\\&=P+O(M\log\alpha/\alpha^2).
\end{align}
For the rest of the sum, since $\alpha-k-r\leq\alpha-r$, Lemma~\ref{lemma_bounds2}~(\ref{lemma_bounds2_nrnk},\ref{lemma_bounds2_qr}) gives $$\sum_{r=\alpha-\lfloor M\log\alpha\rfloor}^{\alpha-k-1}\frac{q_r^2}{n_{\alpha-r}-K}=O\left(\sum_{r=\alpha-\lfloor M\log\alpha\rfloor}^{\alpha-k-1}\frac{\alpha-k-r}{\alpha^2(\alpha-r)}\right)=O(M\log\alpha/\alpha^2).$$

(\ref{lemma_sums_2}) For $k+1=o(\alpha-r)$, Lemma~\ref{lemma_bounds2}~(\ref{lemma_bounds2_nrk},\ref{lemma_bounds2_pr},\ref{lemma_bounds2_qr}) gives $$\frac{q_r^2p_r}{n_{\alpha-r}-K}=\left(1+O\left(\frac{k+1}{\alpha-r}\right)\right)\tfrac{2}{\ell}r\alpha^{-3}=\tfrac{P}{\alpha^2}r+O\left(\frac{M}{(\alpha-r)\alpha^2}\right).$$ For the sum, we get
