	&=(t^*)^C\sum_{t=\lfloor t^*\rfloor+1}^{\ell k}t^{-C}
	\\&\leq\left(\frac{t^*}{\lfloor t^*\rfloor+1}\right)^{C}+(t^*)^C\int_{\lfloor t^*\rfloor+1}^{\ell k}x^{-C}\,\mathrm{d}x,
	\\\int_{\lfloor t^*\rfloor+1}^{\ell k}x^{-C}\,\mathrm{d}x
	&\leq\int_{t^*}^{\infty}x^{-C}\,\mathrm{d}x=\frac{(t^*)^{1-C}}{C-1}.
\end{align}
If $t^*\geq1$, then $(\frac{t^*}{\lfloor t^*\rfloor+1})^C\leq1\leq t^*$. Otherwise, $(\frac{t^*}{\lfloor t^*\rfloor+1})^C=(t^*)^C\leq t^*$, because $C\geq2$. It follows that $\log\Pi^{(u)}\leq(1+\tfrac1{C-1})t^*\leq Ct^*$, which we already showed to be $o(k)$.

